{
  "text": " And then just last but not least, I want to remind you guys that there's a COVID litigation conference in Atlanta next month that I'll be speaking at. Robert Malone will be there. This is put on by Ryan will be there. It's put on by VSRF and Steve Kersh. And it's led by Warner Mendenhall who who's been a lawyer for 30 years. He has a huge law practice and his specialty is literally litigating against fraud, fraud in government, fraud in corporations. And really this conference is for lawyers as well as lay people because I think there are a lot of people. I mean, listen, what's the purpose of this conference guys? With all these policies, some of which I referred to tonight, I mean, millions of lives were affected in COVID, right? From people who small businesses were shut down, which is a property right infringement, travel restrictions, mandates preventing people from going to school or work or making their livelihood, right? You guys know all our stories of me and Paul are freaking careers ended, right? And we're still we're still getting crap from board certifying agencies in our state medical boards. And then unfortunately, the poor patients, of course, right, everybody in the hospitals being subjected to these literally pharmaceutical industry controlled protocols, which don't work and which were dangerous. You know, there's a number of areas of medical negligence in the hospital. For instance, I think it was Warner who told me that there was a study that showed that 25% of the remdesivir infusions were received by patients who did not meet criteria. And you want to know why that might have happened. Maybe there was something called a financial incentive to give remdesivir. And then obviously the medical fraud around the trials. And then there's apparently immense fraud around those paycheck protection plan loans, where I don't know, we spent, I can't remember how many tens of billions of or hundreds of billions of dollars on that. So anyway, it's for lawyers, they're going to teach legal strategy, they're going to share pleadings, you know, case law, legal theory around it. And so I think for lawyers who are interested, you know, one of the things that Warner told me is he wants to incentivize lawyers, he says, there's a lot of work, there's a lot of people that need legal help, because of the damages and suffering that they've gone through, on that he wants to incentivize the lawyers to meet the need of the population. So I think it's a pretty important conference. Like I said, if you're interested in finding a lawyer or learning more about whether there is a case for you, if you've been subjected to any of these horrific intrusions in your life, please feel free to attend.",
